    <string name="tip_got_it">Got it</string>
    <string name="tip_swipe">Swipe anywhere to slide your hatchling. Reach the waves to save it!</string>
    <string name="tip_all_move">Every swipe moves every hatchling at once. They all slide until they bump into something.</string>
    <string name="tip_blocking">Hatchlings stop when they bump into each other. Use one to stop the other!</string>
    <string name="tip_rock">Rocks are stoppers. Slide into a rock to stop right where you need to be.</string>
    <string name="tip_shell">Shells stop hatchlings just like rocks do.</string>
    <string name="tip_gull">Watch the seagull counter. Save everyone before it reaches zero!</string>
    <string name="tip_wet_sand">Wet sand is sticky: a hatchling that slides onto it stops right there.</string>
    <string name="tip_cracked_shell">Cracked shells stop you once, then break into sand.</string>
    <string name="tip_current">Currents push hatchlings the way the arrow points, and they keep sliding.</string>
    <string name="tip_coconut">Coconuts slide too! They make great moving stoppers.</string>
    <string name="tip_pit">Keep hatchlings out of sand pits. Roll a coconut in to fill one up.</string>
    <string name="tip_crab">Crabs scuttle back and forth after every move. They block the way.</string>
    <string name="tip_late_egg">Some eggs hatch later. The new hatchling has to reach the sea too.</string>
    <string name="tip_tide_pool">Slide into a tide pool to pop out of its twin, still moving the same way.</string>
    <string name="tip_gull_shadow">The gull’s shadow glides after each move. Don’t finish a move underneath it!</string>
